  "verdict": "At 64 tasks over 16 repository clusters, the smallest effect this corpus can detect at 80% power is between 25 and 30 points; a literature-sized effect of 4.88 points has power 0.108. Reaching 80% power for that effect needs about 2048 tasks, against the 64 available today. Between-repository effect heterogeneity estimated from R3's measured per-repository deltas is 0.00 points, so the binding constraint is total task count and this audit does not claim repositories are the scarce resource."
